IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pl-types`
IMPORT `pl-eligibility`

-- Parental Leave and Employment Protection Act 1987 — GOAL 3: NOTICES, THE
-- POSITION, AND PROTECTION.
--
--   "When are notices due; on what grounds may the employer show the
--    position cannot be kept open; what holiday pay follows the leave; may
--    the leave end early or be extended; is a dismissal unlawful; and by
--    when must a complaint be made?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1987_129.txt — Parts 4-7,
-- ss 31-71.

§ `Goal 3 — notices, the position, and protection`

§§ `Notices (ss 31-39)`

-- s 35(1) "where an employee fails to give notice under section 31(1)
-- within the time required by section 31(3) or section 33, that employee
-- shall not be entitled to take extended leave under this Act unless— (a)
-- that employee gives a written notice ... and a period of 3 months beginning
-- with the date of the giving of that notice has expired; or (b) the
-- employer ... agrees". (2) not where an incomplete notice was given in time.
-- s 68 (relief for irregularities) is an input: a notice the Authority
-- excuses counts as in time.
@ref ss 35, 68
GIVEN start IS A DATE, `in time` IS A BOOLEAN, notice IS A DATE, agrees IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `extended leave may start on` start `, notice in time:` `in time` `, notice given` notice `, employer agrees:` agrees IF
        `in time`
    OR  agrees
    OR  start AT LEAST `add months` notice 3

-- s 34(2) the employer, "within 7 days after the date on which it comes to
-- that employer's attention that the notice is an incomplete notice"; (3)
-- the employee, "within 14 days after the date on which the employee
-- receives the notice"; s 36(1) the employer, "within 21 days after the
-- receipt of the notice"; s 38 the employer, "Within 21 days after the
-- beginning of an employee's parental leave".
@ref ss 34, 36, 38
GIVEN days IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day, within` days `days after` d MEANS
    `the day` days `days after` d

-- s 37(2) "not less than 21 days' notice in writing of the day on which the
-- employee wishes his or her primary carer leave to begin"; s 39(2) "not
-- less than 21 days' notice in writing" of an early return. FORK F3 again:
-- clear days.
@ref ss 37, 39(2)
GIVEN start IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to give 21 days' notice of a day` start MEANS
    `the day` (0 MINUS 22) `days after` start

-- s 39(1) "not later than 21 days before the date on which the employee's
-- parental leave ends". (3) not if the employment agreement requires longer
-- notice of resignation.
@ref s 39(1)
GIVEN ends IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to say whether the employee will return, leave ending` ends MEANS
    `the day` (0 MINUS 21) `days after` ends

§§ `Keeping the position open (ss 40, 41)`

DECLARE `Grounds the position cannot be kept open` IS ONE OF
    `only a redundancy situation (s 40)`
    `a key position that cannot be temporarily filled, or a redundancy situation (s 41)`

-- s 40(1) a continuous period "(a) that does not exceed 4 weeks ...; and (b)
-- that is the first period of parental leave taken by the employee in
-- respect of the child; and (c) of which the employee's employer has had no
-- less notice than the period of notice required" — the employer must prove
-- a redundancy situation. s 41(1) any other period: "(a) because a temporary
-- replacement is not reasonably practicable due to the key position ...; or
-- (b) because of the occurrence of a redundancy situation."
@ref ss 40, 41
GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER, first IS A BOOLEAN, `notice in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Grounds the position cannot be kept open`
`the grounds the employer may prove, leave of` weeks `weeks, first period:` first `, notice in time:` `notice in time` MEANS
    IF   weeks AT MOST 4 AND first AND `notice in time`
    THEN `only a redundancy situation (s 40)`
    ELSE `a key position that cannot be temporarily filled, or a redundancy situation (s 41)`

§§ `Holiday pay after leave (s 42)`

-- s 42(2) "If an employee becomes entitled to an annual holiday on pay
-- during— (a) a period of parental leave ...; or (b) a period of preference
-- ...; or (c) the period of 12 months commencing with the date on which the
-- employee returns to work after a period of parental leave ... or a period
-- of preference ...,— the employee is, despite anything in section 21 of the
-- Holidays Act 2003, entitled to holiday pay for that holiday only at the
-- rate of the employee's average weekly earnings".
@ref s 42(2)
GIVEN arose IS A DATE, began IS A DATE, returned IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `annual holiday pay is at average weekly earnings only, entitlement arising` arose `, leave began` began `, returned` returned IF
        arose AT LEAST began
    AND CONSIDER returned
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST r THEN arose LESS THAN `add years` r 1

§§ `Ending and extending leave (ss 45-47)`

-- s 45(1) the employee may end leave early "(a) if the employee or the
-- employee's spouse or partner suffers a miscarriage; or (b) if the child is
-- stillborn or dies; or (c) if the employee or the employee's spouse or
-- partner fails to become or ceases to be the primary carer ...; or (d)
-- [(e)] if the employer consents".
@ref s 45(1)
GIVEN miscarriage IS A BOOLEAN, `stillborn or died` IS A BOOLEAN, `no longer carer` IS A BOOLEAN, consents IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may end the leave early, miscarriage:` miscarriage `, stillborn or died:` `stillborn or died` `, not or no longer the primary carer:` `no longer carer` `, employer consents:` consents IF
    miscarriage OR `stillborn or died` OR `no longer carer` OR consents

-- s 45(3)-(4) an extension, with the employer's consent, may not make "(a)
-- ... primary carer leave ... exceed 26 weeks: (b) ... partner's leave ...
-- exceed— (i) 1 week if the employee meets the 6-month employment test: (ii)
-- 2 weeks if the employee meets the 12-month employment test".
@ref s 45(3)-(4)
GIVEN `primary carer leave` IS A BOOLEAN, t IS AN `Employment test`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the longest the leave may be extended to, in weeks, primary carer leave:` `primary carer leave` `, test met` t MEANS
    IF   `primary carer leave`
    THEN 26
    ELSE CONSIDER t
         WHEN `the 12-month employment test` THEN 2
         WHEN `the 6-month employment test`  THEN 1
         WHEN `neither employment test`      THEN 0

-- s 46 the employment "shall, subject to any agreement ..., be deemed to
-- have been at an end as from the day on which the period of parental leave
-- began" if the employee "(a) fails, without good cause, to return to work
-- ...; or (b) informs the employer ... that the employee has decided not to
-- return". s 47 the same if the employee "fails, without reasonable excuse,
-- to take up, on the date specified by the employer or within 7 days
-- thereafter, any position substantially similar ... offered ... during the
-- period of 26 weeks".
@ref ss 46, 47
GIVEN `kept open` IS A BOOLEAN, `no return without good cause` IS A BOOLEAN, `said would not return` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused a similar position without excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employment is deemed ended when the leave began, kept open:` `kept open` `, no return without good cause:` `no return without good cause` `, said would not return:` `said would not return` `, refused a similar position without excuse:` `refused a similar position without excuse` `, agreed otherwise:` `agreed otherwise` IF
        NOT `agreed otherwise`
    AND (    (`kept open` AND (`no return without good cause` OR `said would not return`))
         OR  `refused a similar position without excuse`)

§§ `Dismissal (ss 49-52)`

-- s 49(1) "(c) during the employee's absence on parental leave or during the
-- period of 26 weeks beginning with the day after the date on which any
-- period of parental leave ends."
@ref ss 49(1)(c), 50
GIVEN d IS A DATE, began IS A DATE, ended IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is during the leave or the 26 weeks after it`  d `, leave` began `to` ended IF
        d AT LEAST began
    AND d AT MOST `the day` 182 `days after` ended

DECLARE `Reason for termination` IS ONE OF
    `(a)(i) her pregnancy`
    `(a)(ii) her state of health during pregnancy`
    `(a)(ii) her state of health, materially affected by causes not related to her pregnancy`
    `(b)(i) the employee wishing to take parental leave`
    `(b)(ii) the employee or spouse or partner becoming the primary carer`
    `a substantial reason not related to the pregnancy, the child, or rights under the Act (s 54)`

-- s 49(1) "No employer shall terminate the employment of any employee— (a)
-- by reason of, in the case of a female employee,— (i) her pregnancy; or
-- (ii) her state of health during her pregnancy, unless her state of health
-- ... is materially affected by causes not related to her pregnancy; or (b)
-- by reason of, in the case of any employee,— (i) the employee indicating
-- that the employee wishes to take parental leave ...; or (ii) the employee,
-- or the employee's spouse or partner, becoming the primary carer ...; or
-- (c) during the employee's absence on parental leave or during the period
-- of 26 weeks" after it. (2) It is not a contravention "(a) with the
-- employee's consent; or (b) where solely on account of [the pregnancy or
-- the child] the employee absents himself or herself from work ... for any
-- period which the employee is not entitled to take as leave". The defences
-- of ss 50-52 (redundancy, no similar position, seniority not prejudiced)
-- are inputs. s 54 "Nothing in this Act shall affect any right of an employer
-- to dismiss an employee for a substantial reason not related to" the
-- pregnancy, the child, or the employee's rights: such a dismissal does not
-- contravene s 49, even during the leave or the 26 weeks after.
@ref ss 49-52, 54
@export Whether terminating an employee's employment contravenes s 49(1) of the Parental Leave and Employment Protection Act 1987 (NZ): a termination by reason of pregnancy, pregnancy-related ill health, wishing to take parental leave or becoming the primary carer, or during parental leave or the 26 weeks after it, unless the employee consented, was absent without entitlement, or (for a termination in that time) the employer proves a defence under ss 51 or 52. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Reason for termination`  @desc The reason for the termination
      d IS A DATE  @desc The date of the termination
      began IS A DATE  @desc The first day of the employee's parental leave
      ended IS A DATE  @desc The last day of the employee's parental leave
      consent IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the employee consented
      `absent without entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the employee, solely because of the pregnancy or the child, was absent for a period they were not entitled to take as leave
      defence IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the employer proves the defence in s 51 (during the leave) or s 52 (in the 26 weeks after)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the termination contravenes s 49(1), reason` r `, on` d `, leave` began `to` ended `, consent:` consent `, absent without entitlement:` `absent without entitlement` `, defence proved:` defence IF
        NOT consent
    AND NOT `absent without entitlement`
    AND NOT r EQUALS `a substantial reason not related to the pregnancy, the child, or rights under the Act (s 54)`
    AND (    prohibited
         OR  (`is during the leave or the 26 weeks after it` d `, leave` began `to` ended AND NOT defence))
    WHERE
        prohibited MEANS
               r EQUALS `(a)(i) her pregnancy`
            OR r EQUALS `(a)(ii) her state of health during pregnancy`
            OR r EQUALS `(b)(i) the employee wishing to take parental leave`
            OR r EQUALS `(b)(ii) the employee or spouse or partner becoming the primary carer`

§§ `Complaints and remedies (ss 55, 56, 70C)`

-- s 55(1) "within the preceding 2 months".
@ref s 55(1)
GIVEN terminated IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply for an interim order, terminated` terminated MEANS
    `add months` terminated 2

-- s 56(2) "A parental leave complaint ... shall not be made— (a) after the
-- expiration of 26 weeks from the date on which the subject matter of the
-- complaint arose; or (b) after the expiration of 26 weeks from— (i) the
-- expected date of delivery ...; or (ii) the first date on which either ...
-- became the primary carer ...; or (c) after the expiration of 8 weeks from
-- the expiry of any period of parental leave taken by the employee,—
-- whichever is the later."
@ref s 56(2)
@export The last day to make a parental leave complaint under s 56(2) of the Parental Leave and Employment Protection Act 1987 (NZ): the latest of 26 weeks after the subject matter arose, 26 weeks after the expected date of delivery (or of becoming the primary carer), and 8 weeks after the end of any parental leave. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN arose IS A DATE  @desc The date the subject matter of the complaint arose
      c IS A Child  @desc The child: whether born to the person or spouse, the expected date of delivery, and the date of becoming the primary carer
      `leave ended` IS A MAYBE DATE  @desc The last day of the parental leave, if any was taken
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to make a parental leave complaint, arising` arose `, child` c `, leave ended` `leave ended` MEANS
    IF a GREATER THAN latest2 THEN a ELSE latest2
    WHERE
        a MEANS `the day` 182 `days after` arose
        b MEANS `the day` 182 `days after` (`the date the tests look back from, for` c)
        e MEANS CONSIDER `leave ended`
                WHEN JUST x THEN `the day` 56 `days after` x
                WHEN NOTHING THEN b
        latest2 MEANS IF b GREATER THAN e THEN b ELSE e

-- s 70C(2) "An objection must be lodged ... within 28 days after the
-- determination or demand notice is served".
@ref s 70C(2)
GIVEN served IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to object, served` served MEANS
    `the day` 28 `days after` served

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 1-1B, 2A-2AD, 2B, 2C, 3, 5, 6A, 10, 12-14, 16, 20, 22, 29, 30A, 30C, 30F-30H, 32, 33, 34(1), 36(3)-(4), 43, 44, 48, 53, 54, 57-59, 64-68, 70, 70A, 70B, 70D-70G, 71, 71A-71C, 71CC, 71CD, 71P-71R, 71S-71W, 71ZA, 72, 72A, 72D, 73-77, Schedule 1AA cls 1-4, Schedule 1
`provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "ss 1-1B title, purpose, outline", "ss 2A-2AD multiple employments and self-employment (each employment counted separately)",
         "s 2B multiple children (treated as 1 child)", "s 2C, Schedule 1AA cls 1-4 transitional (earlier children refused)", "s 3 Crown bound",
         "s 5 aggregate with leave under other provisions", "s 6A service restarts on return", "s 10 when primary carer leave begins",
         "ss 12-14 start by agreement, by certificate, by the employer", "s 16 temporary transfer", "s 20, 22 when partner's leave begins",
         "s 29 consecutive or concurrent extended leave", "s 30A object of Part 3A", "s 30C contents of a request", "ss 30F-30H challenges, Labour Inspectors, mediation",
         "s 32 contents of an extended leave notice", "s 33 notice where not the birth parent", "s 34(1) incomplete notice", "s 36(3)-(4) notice to a (b)(iii) carer; disputes",
         "s 43 continuity of service", "s 44 superannuation contributions", "s 48 temporary replacements", "s 53 redundancy payments", "s 54 dismissal for cause",
         "ss 57-59, 64-67 complaint procedure and remedies", "s 68 irregularities (an input)", "s 70 enforcement of judgments",
         "ss 70A, 70B, 70D-70G Labour Inspector determinations and demand notices", "s 71 State employees",
         "ss 71A-71C purpose, Armed Forces, interpretation", "s 71CC (no text)", "s 71CD return to work by a self-employed person",
         "ss 71P-71R non-statutory entitlements, public money, method of payment", "ss 71S-71W backdating, employer notice, notifying return, information",
         "s 71ZA delegation", "s 72 contracting out of holiday pay", "s 72A counting hours (an input)", "s 72D ERA for the self-employed",
         "ss 73-77 regulations, repeal, transitional, savings", "Schedule 1 change of employer (an input to the employment tests)"
